    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, containing both scenarios). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `registrationDate` field to owners: supplied on create it's kept, omitted it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this makes the field accepted on `POST /api/owners` and returned on `GET`. The `format: date` maps to `java.time.LocalDate` in the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`, getter/setter, and the `LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** \u2014 a new OfficeFloor step that, following the AGENTS.md conventions, reads the built `Owner` via `@Val` and sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when it's null (a supplied date is left untouched).\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `defaultRegistrationDate` step into the pipeline between `build` and `save` (under the same `transaction` governance).\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nBoth acceptance scenarios pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (preserves `2020-06-15`).",
